## Defects found and resolved during UAT

| Defect | Severity | Resolution |
|---|---|---|
| Backend fallback unreachable after raising HTTP 503 | Critical | Endpoint now returns fallback data on live OpenAQ failure. |
| Backend hard-coded `PM2.5` / `µg/m³` for all pollutants | Critical | Live GeoJSON now derives pollutant name and unit from the selected pollutant configuration. |
| PM2.5 regional reference/score reused conceptually for other pollutants | High | Exposure/reference fields are now PM2.5-only. |
| Chart tooltip always displayed PM2.5 / µg/m³ | High | Dynamic pollutant/unit formatter added. |
| “Trend” label implied historical time-series not present in the data | High | Renamed to latest selected-city measurement comparison. |
| Duplicate city listbox IDs | Medium | Unique React `useId()` IDs added. |
| City combobox keyboard interaction incomplete | Medium | Arrow Up/Down, Enter, Escape and active descendant implemented. |
| Fixed-width city selector could overflow narrow screens | Medium | Responsive full-width mobile behavior added. |
| Header could display LIVE DATA after errors | Medium | State label now distinguishes error/fallback/empty/live/loading. |
| City comparison divide-by-zero produced misleading `0%` | Medium | Explicit unavailable percentage message added. |

## Acceptance conclusion

All required UAT areas are represented, all discovered gate-blocking defects were remediated in the acceptance build, and the automated acceptance harness reports no failures. The resulting workflow degrades safely when upstream services are unavailable and does not mislabel PM2.5 data as another pollutant.

